kinds: hard: every execution in which both instances occur has them in this order, under the premises; conditional: only when the condition holds; observed-only: no rule of this revision orders them, a run record may show an order
closure: hard_before and fixed_early_proved follow hard edges only; a conditional edge makes the path conditional (conditional_before, fixed_early_candidate) and is never in the hard closure; observed-only edges are not followed; a caller-dependent spawn call (in a function a call of a spawn operation's chain calls) is followed from a thread only to the threads that thread's own outer spawn calls create
